  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) achieved 0.507 accuracy, far exceeding image-only config_014 (0.332), confirming multimodal fusion is essential. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (scgpt) and don't know whether the RNA representation quality is a bottleneck. Question: config_019 changes only the RNA encoder from scgpt to scvi_n200 while holding image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), and fusion (concat) identical to config_002. This clean one-variable comparison isolates the RNA encoder's contribution. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is a fundamental design choice that determines the quality of the transcriptomic representation fed into fusion. With 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether scgpt or scvi_n200 is superior early will guide all subsequent multimodal experiments and prevent wasting budget on suboptimal encoder combinations. If scvi_n200 matches or exceeds scgpt, it opens a large branch of configurations; if scgpt is clearly better, we can confidently exploit scgpt-based variants."
}

